D.C. and Puerto Rico. The company was founded in 1972 and is headquartered in Burlington, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael B. O'Sullivan | CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 17K people. Revenue per employee of $661K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Burlington Stores, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $15.8B market cap on $11.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $172M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.02\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 57% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5736818874497982},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital s